WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.390
SCP-1730 is one of the biggest threats the
Foundation has ever faced.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.130
SCP-1730 does not exist.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.630
It was June 5th when the compound was first
discovered.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:16.000
A large complex of structures in rural Texas,
about fifteen kilometers northwest of the

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Mexican border.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.189
Located in Big Bend Ranch State Park, it was
easily the biggest structure in the area.

00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:25.130
But there was no record of any such structure
ever being built.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:31.550
A massive network of power stations, containment
facilities, and research buildings, SCP-1730

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.950
looked like it had been abandoned for a long
time.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.950
The exterior was degraded, but the building
was still operating.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.210
A power generator had been running for an
indeterminate amount of time, even as the

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.800
infrastructure degraded.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.860
Power flickered through the sight and fuel
leaked frequently.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.280
But there was one detail that attracted the
attention of SCP brass.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:55.960
SCP-1730 bore identifying markings linking
it to Foundation Site 13, a research facility

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.060
that was marked for construction near Nome,
Alaska.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:03.720
But Site 13 had never been built, having been
abandoned in the planning stages.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:08.390
So why is it in the middle of Texas, fully
constructed and long abandoned?

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:12.020
The Foundation needed to know more, and they
needed their best to investigate.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.630
It was time to call in the “Game Wardens”.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:19.450
Apollo-3, the mobile task force used to investigate
dangerous sites, was brought in, and five

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:24.650
elite agents were briefed and sent in - Ross,
Houston, Noah, Ohalo, and Vigo.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:28.950
It didn’t take long for them to discover
that something was very wrong with the site

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.420
of SCP-1730.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.959
The facility was located in the middle of
south Texas - but the local flora surrounding

00:01:34.959 --> 00:01:37.520
it was native to Nome, Alaska.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.200
Something had transplanted a building that
shouldn’t exist to another place and time.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.159
Commander Ross ordered his men to enter, with
Houston taking lead, and they discovered that

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:48.590
entry led down a long staircase.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:53.009
They descended slowly, following a strange
light that no one could identify - but had

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:57.060
a sudden shock when they discovered that the
basement of the staircase was missing.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:00.920
The light suddenly stopped, and it became
so dark that it was impossible to see what

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.789
lay beyond the staircase.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:07.299
Upon probing the inky black void at the base
of the staircase, they determined it wasn’t

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:08.940
a fog or shadow.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:09.950
It was a liquid.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:11.450
And it was rising.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:14.680
Ross ordered his men back, but Houston was
in too deep.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.450
He couldn’t break free from the inky black
liquid.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.840
The men pulled him away, and got him free
- but his legs were gone!

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.950
Not ripped off, because there was no blood
anywhere.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.770
Smoothly cut off, as if they were never there.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:30.180
And as they put Houston down, he stood up
- on phantom legs.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:35.270
He didn’t feel any pain, but everyone could
tell something was very wrong with this place.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:39.080
And the messages they started seeing on the
wall made clear they weren’t the only ones

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.080
who knew it.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.440
“What Happened to Site 13?”

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:42.440
“Death Here”

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:43.510
“Not My Body”

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.510
“Bleed”

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:49.920
There had been other people - or things - inside
SCP-1730, and they wanted anyone who entered

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.230
to know that this was a very dangerous place
to be.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.420
As they advanced down the hall back towards
the entrance, they saw what looked like a

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:57.620
person in the distance.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:01.390
But as they approached, it became clear this
wasn’t another explorer.

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:06.230
It was an old, horribly disfigured corpse
seemingly attached to the wall.

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:09.950
Not by chains - but fused into the wall in
unnatural ways.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:13.980
At first, the team seemed unconcerned - recognizing
the corpse as someone named Zachary.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:19.310
Fortunately, command back at base realized
this as the effects of some sort of cognitohazard

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.780
- a mental infection - in the base.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.290
They uploaded a filter to their helmets, and
the team recoiled in horror at the site in

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.290
front of them.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.940
But the horrors were just beginning.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:32.860
They turned around to see a shimmering, humanoid
entity in the hallway behind them.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.770
As it approached, its footsteps distorted
the hallway around.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:41.410
It pulled AP-3 Noah towards it, without touching
him, and as the soldier was pulled into its

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.010
clutches, his body started to distort.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:47.820
Vigo was next, being grabbed by the arm by
a long appendage, and his arm started to change

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:48.820
color and distort.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.050
But the foundation sent Apollo-3 in prepared.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:56.510
Houston produced a portable reality anchor,
designed to handle reality-warping entities,

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.260
and with a flash of red light the creature
was revealed.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.340
It was a horribly elongated humanoid that
only existed for a second before the reality

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.520
anchor erased it and restored the hallway
to its normal state.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.130
Vigo would recover, with the strange red color
in his arm fading eventually.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:13.410
Noah wasn’t so lucky.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.510
He was already dead.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:18.100
And had been fused into the wall just like
the unfortunate corpse.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:22.320
These horrors had been encountered just by
trying to return to the entrance, so it was

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:27.510
clear the only smart thing to do was to descend
further into the facilities and get some answers.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:32.010
As they advanced, not encountering any other
supernatural entities, they saw more evidence

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:34.910
of the dark things that had occurred in Site
13.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:40.000
The infirmary had been torn apart, a cafeteria
had been melted into slag, and a large group

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.700
of containment cells ended with a section
called “Olympia Class”.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:49.370
But while most of the other cells were standard
sized, these were over 100 meters high.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:54.260
What had the foundation - or whoever ran this
place - been keeping in these cells?

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:58.260
They would get more answers as they made their
way down another hall, where they saw a single

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.250
television still working and illuminating
their hallway.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.910
At first the television flickered, but the
image soon cleared, and the agents were able

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.470
to see what was broadcasting.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:08.340
It was the interior of a containment cell.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.980
And there was someone in it.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:15.430
And they recognized them as one of the most
dangerous beings contained by the SCP Foundation

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:16.450
- Bobble the Clown.

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:22.050
A predatory supernatural clown that inhabits
a children’s TV show, Bobble the Clown was

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:26.770
broadcast by an unknown source and could only
be seen by children under ten.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:31.139
Originally seeming to be a normal kids’
show about a clown, every episode eventually

00:05:31.139 --> 00:05:35.870
devolved into the murderous Bobble teaching
the kids how to do horrible things like arson

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:36.870
or torture.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.870
The Foundation eventually captured and isolated
Bobble’s broadcast, but the clown remained

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.510
hostile and vicious.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:43.510
Not here.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:48.320
As the team talked to the Bobble trapped in
the mysterious Site 13, it became clear that

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.500
this clown was broken by whatever it had experienced.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:55.669
It rambled, it hid from the camera, and it
was clearly terrified as it told the team

00:05:55.669 --> 00:05:57.060
about the horrors of the site.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:01.350
And it seemed to recognize the agents as something
familiar - but not completely familiar.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:05.340
It claimed to be able to smell them - and
said they smelled different.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:10.020
As Bobble rambled on and on, the agents learned
about a man named Emerson, who ran the site.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:13.680
Like the Foundation, he was obsessed with
containing the strange and dangerous entities

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:14.680
in the world.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.450
But unlike the foundation, he didn’t just
want to protect the world from them.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:19.450
He hated them.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.310
The entities in Site 13 didn’t even have
numbers - they might identify by them.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:26.770
Emerson wanted to use them up however he wanted
and dispose of them - in something Bobble

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.760
called the “meat grinder”.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:32.730
Entities that outlived their usefulness were
taken down below - and none were ever heard

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:33.730
from again.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:38.760
It was directly counter to every SCP Foundation
policy - but this site had clearly been performing

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.780
these horrible experiments for years.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:41.780
How?

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:43.210
And why hadn’t anyone ever heard of it?

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:47.090
The team continued to make their way into
the facility, but their signals were lost

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.949
as they entered the cryogenics unit.

00:06:48.949 --> 00:06:52.520
By the time contact had been restored, they
were no longer alone.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:53.630
There were survivors.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:57.330
Both agents of the foundation - and survivors
of the facility.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.710
And they were angry.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:02.390
With no way out and massively outnumbered,
they called for backup.

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:07.419
Mobile Task Force T-5, also known as “Samsara”,
was reserved for the heavy-duty missions.

00:07:07.419 --> 00:07:12.290
They’re an elite group of practically immortal
cyborgs fashioned from the flesh of a god,

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:17.540
and equipped with further cybernetic enhancements
to eliminate Keter-level threats and to protect

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.360
themselves from cognitohazards.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:23.520
They were sent in through a drainage gate
to look for survivors and neutralize whatever

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.520
lay within.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:28.300
They didn’t know what to expect, but they
knew one thing - no one who had been sent

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.300
in had come out.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.960
It wasn’t long before they realized how
dangerous this mission would be.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:37.669
As they came across some large gated drainage
pipes, they could see at least twenty charred

00:07:37.669 --> 00:07:42.010
bodies of humanoids pushed up against the
gate, some reaching their hands through.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:46.670
Whatever had happened in Site 13, these unfortunate
beings had been desperate to escape.

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:50.680
As they made their way down the drainage pipe,
they could feel it getting hotter, as if they

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.030
were nearing an energy source.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:55.570
And there was one other odd thing about the
pipe.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.280
It was draining inward, not out.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:01.810
They made their way to a control room, where
many of the consoles had been destroyed.

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:05.530
Looking through a window, their view was obscured
by a mysterious black mass.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:09.740
On the control panels, they could read terms
like “incinerator” and “body pit access”.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:13.790
They split up, trying to find answers, but
found many of their accesses blocked by the

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:14.820
black mass.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:19.460
As the T-5 task force argued over their next
move, they were startled by a sudden jolt.

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.700
The giant mass had started moving.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:26.540
The team watched as the mass spun, revealing
a giant turbine, which turned the inky substance

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:30.610
into a fine slurry that was then scorched
by giant streaks of fire.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:35.190
One of T-5 shot open the glass chamber, allowing
the team to get closer - and blasting them

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:36.500
with a wave of heat.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:41.000
As they descended into the chamber, they could
see a massive plant-like structure overhead,

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.690
which started to shake.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:47.210
Suddenly, thousands of glowing pods were released
from the massive plant, and each one lit up

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.690
and let the team view the chamber more clearly.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:53.190
But it was what was inside the pods that was
more disturbing.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:58.190
Each pod had a humanoid shape inside, seemingly
reaching towards the team, until they hit

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:00.690
the slurry below - and the shadows went dark.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:04.750
The team descended to investigate the slurry,
when something started to leak out of the

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:05.750
walls.

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:07.230
Looking at it, they could see something moving
within.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:11.430
One of the team members picked the wriggling
object out of the black liquid - and it took

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:12.770
a bite out of his hand!

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:16.880
It was a leech - and there were thousands
more of them moving towards the slurry, consuming

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:17.880
it.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.160
And as the leeches ate, they started growing.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:24.190
They seemed to be moving in unison, communicating
with a larger being lurking at the base of

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:25.190
the slurry.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.900
A larger leech, a queen?

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:27.900
Or something else?

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.529
The team wasn’t sticking around to find
out.

00:09:30.529 --> 00:09:34.890
They beat a hurried escape from the leech
room, finding themselves in another hallway.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:39.240
Whatever the black substance was, the entities
who had been here had used it, scrawling “Blood”

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.399
on the walls over and over again.

00:09:41.399 --> 00:09:44.899
Occasionally, they would come across a drained
corpse covered in the black fluid.

00:09:44.899 --> 00:09:46.780
Had the leeches bled them dry?

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:50.650
The facility was so sprawling that the team
knew that if they wanted any chance of navigating

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.290
it safely, they needed to get the lay of the
land.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.230
They needed to find the control center.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:58.920
The door read “Stairs to Cryonics” and
the leeches were nowhere to be found.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:00.110
It seemed like a safe path.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:04.410
But as soon as the team entered, the temperature
dropped drastically, to well below where it

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.560
would be safe for a human to survive.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:10.300
The team’s internal heating system kicked
in, saving their lives, but that wasn’t

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.390
the only threat.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:15.230
The team was about to encounter exactly what
Site 13 was keeping locked up.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:18.710
As soon as they entered the room, sound ceased
to work.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:23.170
The filters in their gear were overloaded,
and the team saw warnings around the room.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:24.170
“Silence”

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:25.170
“Don’t Look”

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:29.290
A massive, multi-limbed figure emerged, with
each of its sixty arms moving independently.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:34.590
The creature had no head, but a large circular
structure covered with ancient glowing symbols.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:38.149
Whatever it was, it was ancient, all-powerful
- and deadly.

00:10:38.149 --> 00:10:42.020
The team scrambled to get away, as the glyphs
on the creature burned white hot.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:43.660
Anyone who touched it was burned.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:47.260
Anyone who looked too long at it felt their
optical implants burn out.

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:52.110
The symbols on the creature were indecipherable,
but one word was clear and printed in English.

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:53.110
“EMERSON”

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:58.100
Site 13 was from another world, another timeline
where the SCP foundation evolved into something

00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.100
horrible.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:03.520
Ruled over by Elliott Emerson, it tortured
its captured beings, and eventually killed

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:06.140
most of them in the horrors of the incinerators.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:10.720
When an escape threatened to destroy the facility,
Emerson successfully activated a device that

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:13.330
removed the facility from their world - into
ours.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:17.589
Of course, as any avid follower of the SCP
Foundation will know, there’s far more to

00:11:17.589 --> 00:11:18.850
the story than this.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:23.410
Emerson may have been the start of Site 13’s
problems, but he was far from the end.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.200
It’s the mission of the century.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:29.790
A daring rescue into the depths of one of
the most dangerous locations in the multiverse:

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:36.160
Site 13, otherwise known as SCP – 1730.When
the impossible Site 13 was first discovered,

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:40.050
multiple Mobile Task Forces were sent to plumb
its depths and none returned.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:44.610
They were greeted to a labyrinthine nightmare,
littered with deadly cognitohazards, escaped

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:47.900
SCPs, and mysterious, murderous leeches.

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:51.000
Some were trapped, along with the civilians
they were sent to rescue.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.990
Others were killed or changed in unimaginable
ways.

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:58.200
Mobile Task Force Apollo-3, also known as
“The Game Wardens”, had been sent in on

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:02.851
a rescue mission when they encountered a horrifying
sight: The captured broadcast of Bobble The

00:12:02.851 --> 00:12:07.490
Clown, a dangerous SCP known for corrupting
and destroying children through its deadly

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:08.490
messages.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.640
But this Bobble was different.

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:14.360
Much like everything from Site 13, this Bobble
came from an entirely different dimension,

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:18.900
and he had terrifying information to relay:
In the universe where Site 13 originated,

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:23.209
the site’s psychopathic director, one Elliot
Emerson, had struck a deal with the Global

00:12:23.209 --> 00:12:27.950
Occult Coalition – a controversial government
group who intends to “protect” humanity

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:30.640
by killing anomalies rather than containing
them.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:36.209
Emerson had converted his site into an unethical,
unrestrained slaughterhouse, and was incinerating

00:12:36.209 --> 00:12:39.310
SCPs by the hundred in a so-called Body Pit.

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:43.640
But Emerson’s game of death came back and
bit him, snapping the threads of reality and

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:47.600
turning the entire site into a dimensionally
displaced super-anomaly.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:51.080
The Game Wardens realized they were in way
over their heads.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.830
Their chances of surviving this place were
dropping by the second, and if they wanted

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:59.000
any chance of succeeding in their mission,
they needed backup, so Site Command called

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:02.130
in MTF Tau-5, aka “Samsara.”

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:07.110
Calling in Samsara for a run-of-the-mill collection
mission is like using a bazooka to kill a

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:12.000
housefly, but for a case as severe as 1730,
their skills were not only nice to have but

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.000
vital.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:17.560
Samsara are among the best of the best: Immortal
cybernetic clones forged from the flesh of

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:22.519
a god, equipped with weaponry and technology
that could surpass even that of other elite

00:13:22.519 --> 00:13:23.950
Mobile Task Force units.

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:28.260
The four members of Samsara are so adept at
what they do that they earned the nickname

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:29.840
“Power Rangers” among their peers.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:34.670
The remaining Game Wardens knew that with
Samsara on the case, they may actually survive

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:37.670
this thing after all, they just needed to
hold out.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:42.589
Samsara arrived on site not long after, packing
some serious technological heat – including

00:13:42.589 --> 00:13:48.120
arm-mounted incendiary cannons, shock-absorbing
leg extensions, heat-resistant plating, and

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:53.180
built-in SCRAMBLE adaptations within their
eyes to ward off the deadly cognitohazards.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.810
Everyone involved was in for the fight of
their lives.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:14:00.740
The four Samsara agents – Irantu, Nanku,
Munru, and Onru – entered via a drainage

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:04.760
gate in one of the office buildings above
ground and began their descent inside.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:09.020
After observing numerous charred bodies, they
deduced that there must be a massive incinerator

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:10.370
somewhere on site.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.810
Emerson’s incinerator.

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:15.730
Theorizing this was connected to the “Body
Pit” they kept hearing about, they descended

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:18.430
further, feeling the temperature rise as they
did so.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:23.830
Due to the anomalous nature of 1730, nothing
inside made any kind of logical sense.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:28.430
Caused by a reality-warping machine known
as THRESHER, the internal geography of Site

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.640
13 was subject to constant shifts.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.959
The team then split up to cover more ground
– Munro and Nanku continued to follow the

00:14:34.959 --> 00:14:39.740
pipes and the heat towards the furnace, while
Irantu and Onru broke away to explore what

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:41.630
lay beyond a weak wall.

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:45.700
After busting through the wall, Irantu and
Onru explored several empty office blocks

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:49.890
before finding their way into a control room
with a glass observation deck.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:53.870
While the window was obscured by garbage and
human corpses, signage indicated that the

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.910
incinerator and the body pit were directly
below them.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:01.329
The team once again reconvened, and managed
to activate the incinerator, which shredded

00:15:01.329 --> 00:15:06.660
the mass stuck inside with several large turbines
before burning the resulting slurry, the same

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:10.350
process that had happened to so many anomalies
under Emerson’s watch.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:15.120
With the path cleared, Samsara decided to
descend via the incinerator, using the drainage

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:17.089
pipe as a kind of makeshift tunnel.

00:15:17.089 --> 00:15:19.579
Eventually, they happened upon the leeches.

00:15:19.579 --> 00:15:24.959
Large, black, and hungry, these creatures
seemed to infest 1730 by the thousand.

00:15:24.959 --> 00:15:29.070
Anywhere that blood or drainage runoff could
be found, the leeches could be found, too.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:32.970
They didn’t appear to have any connection
to an anomaly previously secured and contained

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:33.970
by the Foundation.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:38.029
They squeezed and wriggled through the cracks
in the walls, searching for fresh blood.

00:15:38.029 --> 00:15:42.519
Onru detected that the leeches all moved with
a kind of collective purpose, suggesting a

00:15:42.519 --> 00:15:44.240
telepathic hive mind.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:48.950
Onru was able to tap into this hive mind using
her cybernetic enhancements, and map the chaotic

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:53.070
geography of 1730 through the leech colony’s
collective knowledge.

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:56.910
With this new advantage, they could add a
second goal to this rescue mission: Find the

00:15:56.910 --> 00:16:01.890
THRESHER device causing all the instability,
and potentially reduce power to it if possible.

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:05.680
But they were on the clock to save the other
survivors, as those leeches were sure to get

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:07.639
hungry for warm blood soon.

00:16:07.639 --> 00:16:11.440
They followed the leeches down the most direct
path towards the survivors.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:15.370
On the way, they encountered a horrifying
creature: The many-limbed humanoid nightmare

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:20.560
that functions as Emerson’s eternal punishment,
his charred body tied screaming and alive

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:23.260
to the platform where the monster’s head
should be.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:27.420
They managed to make it past the monster before
finally rendezvousing with Captain Hollis

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:32.019
of Mobile Task Force Zeta-9, otherwise known
as the “Mole Rats”, as well as the Game

00:16:32.019 --> 00:16:33.570
Wardens and the other survivors.

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:39.100
There were 27 surviving members of Site 13
staff, many of which had severe injuries – making

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:42.550
it even harder to transport them back to safety
through hazardous terrain.

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:45.459
And to make matters worse, the leeches were
back.

00:16:45.459 --> 00:16:49.779
The team quickly decided that the best route
out of here was directly past the THRESHER,

00:16:49.779 --> 00:16:53.540
where they could reduce power to the machine
for just long enough to create a stable path

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.540
of escape.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:58.240
Nanku opened fire on a hoard of approaching
leeches with a flamethrower, and everyone

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.270
began running for their lives.

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:02.730
It was a final, make-or-break dash to safety.

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:07.689
However, their advance was soon stopped by
a strange, robed creature drawing a cognitohazardous

00:17:07.689 --> 00:17:09.280
meme on the wall with its claws.

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:14.190
When the team attempted to engage, it attacked,
exposing additional deadly memes and the dangerous

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:15.670
effects of its single white eye.

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:18.350
And we’re not talking about internet memes
here.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:22.260
These are symbols and information that are
often deadly to even bear witness to, and

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:26.829
for you or I, this would be a real threat,
but not to a team equipped with goggles containing

00:17:26.829 --> 00:17:29.120
cognitohazard filter technology.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.140
The battle was cut short when the floor collapsed
underneath them and this creature was devoured

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:39.390
by something even larger and more monstrous:
A gigantic black leech covered in huge, red

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:40.390
eyes.

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:44.450
Its entrance caused thousands of leeches to
spill out into the hall, as the monster screeched

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.720
and slithered its tentacles after them.

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:52.100
Allow us to introduce you to Elijah, also
known as The Leech Boy, and a pivotal component

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:54.880
of the very existence of SCP – 1730.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:58.960
He was a boy with the mind of a toddler, but
he had the strange ability to absorb blood

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:02.150
through people’s skin – hence his nickname,
“Leech Boy.”

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:06.870
One of the doctors in Site 13, Dr. Hadley,
took pity on Elijah – after all, he didn’t

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.549
choose to be the way he was.

00:18:08.549 --> 00:18:10.990
Director Emerson didn’t share Hadley’s
sympathy.

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:14.890
His orders to exterminate all anomalies included
humanoids like Elijah.

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:19.490
When Hadley protested, Emerson had her beaten
within an inch of her life while other dissenters

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:20.490
were shot.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:25.180
Dr. Hadley, disgusted by the inhumanity of
her superiors, devised the perfect revenge.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:29.450
She sabotaged the incinerator and the body
pit, allowing a mass containment breach that

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:31.530
flooded the site with deadly anomalies.

00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:35.920
Young Elijah ended up consuming the slurry
of the other shredded anomalies, causing him

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:40.880
to mutate into a powerful monster, a behemoth
of a leech who gave birth to and controlled

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:41.880
all others.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:46.290
It was Hadley’s revenge that caused Emerson
to panic and activate THRESHER, leading to

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:51.000
the rift in reality and the creation of 1730,
and – by extension – all the problems

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.940
faced by our heroes today.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.820
Samsara and the others fled Leech Boy and
began taking a different escape route.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:01.080
However, while en route, they encountered
the dreaded Crystal Butterflies – a dangerous

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.340
SCP capable of destroying organic matter with
a mere touch.

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:09.309
Irantu stepped up to bat, roasting the creatures
with his arm-mounted incinerator and taking

00:19:09.309 --> 00:19:11.840
extreme damage to his body in the process.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:13.150
But they didn’t have time to rest.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:16.530
With the butterflies disposed of, they kept
moving, heading towards the THRESHER.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:20.080
But not all the SCPs were necessarily working
against them.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:23.919
Bobble the Clown came in handy at the next
checkpoint, manifesting in the monitor of

00:19:23.919 --> 00:19:26.549
an electronic door and opening the way through.

00:19:26.549 --> 00:19:29.970
As they continued on their journey, they had
to fight off frequent attacks from leeches,

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:33.010
losing some of the task force members in the
process.

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:36.890
They were also forced to face off against
a number of other anomalies in order to survive

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:43.630
– such as SCP – 2316 manifesting as floating
bodies beneath them, and SCP – 1370, which

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:47.270
used a huge, mechanized body to attack the
team of survivors.

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:50.470
That was all just a warm-up for the true final
battle, though.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:54.669
The floor shattered beneath them, and out
of an impossibly huge chamber, the monster

00:19:54.669 --> 00:19:59.500
that had once been Elijah wriggled free – reaching
for them with huge tentacles and shrieking

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:01.260
from its thousand-toothed maw.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:06.140
It was at least two hundred meters tall, and
barely reacted to any amount of firepower.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:10.360
It seemed like they were all doomed, until
Captain Hollis had a truly crazy idea.

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:14.960
With the help of Samsara, she led the bloodthirsty
abomination down through the cryonics center

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:17.320
and into an Olympia-class testing chamber.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:21.990
There, as the Leech Boy was bearing down on
them, Hollis opened the gates to two adjacent

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.890
containment cells, and something beyond incredible
happened.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:30.080
Two of the most powerful SCPs ever known – the
giant, sword-wielding gate guardian, and the

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:34.890
reality bending cosmic deer, SCP – 2845
– entered the arena.

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:39.421
What followed was one of the most epic showdowns
in the history of the SCP Foundation, as the

00:20:39.421 --> 00:20:43.670
Deer and the Gate Guardian went to battle
against the all-devouring Leech.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:47.000
While the monsters fought, Hollis ordered
her team to get the rest of the survivors

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:48.000
to safety.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:52.020
She and Munru of the Samsara team remained
behind to prevent any of the anomalies from

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:56.890
escaping as the entire base began sinking
into the ground from the combined forces of

00:20:56.890 --> 00:21:01.210
the battle raging around them and the THRESHER’s
continued onslaught on reality.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:05.710
Even if the survivors escaped, would the anomalous
developments inside Site 13 escape and wreak

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:07.290
havoc on the world at large?

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:12.130
That’s when Hollis received a vision, a
horrific, charred, post-apocalyptic world

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:16.210
roamed by inconceivably powerful entities
and nightmare gods.

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:19.510
It was a vision so horrific that just seeing
it nearly broke her mind.

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:23.700
She knew what she had to do – the only way
she could truly defeat this terrible place

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:25.740
and ensure safety for mankind.

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:29.760
While Leech Boy, the Gate Guardian, and the
Deer continued their battle for the ages,

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.840
Hollis ran to THRESHER and forced the machine
into overdrive.

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:37.570
Up above, the remaining members of Samsara,
the Mole Rats, and the Game Wardens escorted

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:39.450
the survivors to safety.

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:43.830
Downstairs, THRESHER emitted a blinding white
light as the system began to overload.

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:48.210
In her final moments, all Hollis could do
was laugh – perhaps it was a laugh of pure

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:51.250
insanity, of a mind broken by the horror she
witnessed.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:55.309
Or perhaps it was a laugh of victory, knowing
that in spite of the immense powers all around

00:21:55.309 --> 00:21:56.309
her, she had won the day.

00:21:56.309 --> 00:22:01.570
She had saved not only the survivors and her
teammates, but possibly all of humanity.

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:03.460
And all it cost her was everything.

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:08.590
Outside, the survivors had reached a safe
distance when the entirety of Site 13 imploded

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:10.320
in a final brilliant flash.

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:15.290
When the dust cleared SCP-1730 was gone, all
that was left was an immense crater where

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:17.450
the impossible base should have once been.

00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:21.320
Captain Hollis had done it – through overloading
the THRESHER machine, she’d taken this anomaly

00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:24.070
out of the world the exact same way it had
entered.

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:28.299
It was torn from its moorings on our earth
and kicked into the infinity of spacetime,

00:22:28.299 --> 00:22:32.040
perhaps never to be seen again, along with
everything it contained.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:34.990
SCP – 1730 was reclassified to “neutralized.”

00:22:34.990 --> 00:22:39.150
Of course, the Foundation would have plenty
of other anomalies to pursue soon after, but

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:42.251
the nightmare of Emerson’s Site 13 was over
once and for all.

00:22:42.251 --> 00:22:50.730
A light shines above a metal table, with a
chair positioned on either side.

00:22:50.730 --> 00:22:56.120
This is the isolated, hermetically-sealed
interview chamber of Provisional Site 23.

00:22:56.120 --> 00:23:00.960
Outside the room waits two shell-shocked human
Mobile Task Force members, another with invisible

00:23:00.960 --> 00:23:05.550
ghost legs, three powerful cyborgs, and a
scientist from another dimension.

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:10.559
They’re all here to talk about one thing:
The nightmare that unfolded at Site 13, also

00:23:10.559 --> 00:23:13.400
known as SCP - 1730.

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:17.900
Everyone thinks they know the story: A mysterious
site suddenly appears in Texas, seeming to

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:22.509
exactly match the blueprint for an abandoned
site that’s supposed to be in Nome, Alaska.

00:23:22.509 --> 00:23:27.080
What started as a simple anomalous location
turned out to be an epic horror from another

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:28.080
dimension.

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:32.430
The task forces sent in by the Foundation
were either massacred or trapped inside, and

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:37.000
those who survived reported seeing unspeakable
carnage inside the base including a death

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.620
machine designed to destroy anomalies.

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:44.210
And that’s not all - as a result of the
mysterious Thresher machine, the entire location

00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:48.740
had been transformed into a shifting, spatial
anomaly filled with creatures straight out

00:23:48.740 --> 00:23:54.179
of a nightmare - from giant, telepathic leech
monsters, to huge, multi-limbed Demi Gods

00:23:54.179 --> 00:23:58.350
that would eternally punish the site’s murderous
director, Elliot Emerson.

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:02.410
It was only through the combined might of
three different Mobile Task Forces - including

00:24:02.410 --> 00:24:07.610
the legendary Samsara - and the sacrifice
of brave Captain Hollis that this cursed location

00:24:07.610 --> 00:24:12.539
was finally flung into a different dimension,
neutralizing the threat it posed to our reality.

00:24:12.539 --> 00:24:16.910
But for the SCP Foundation, the story doesn’t
end with neutralization - there’s still

00:24:16.910 --> 00:24:18.910
plenty more questions that need answering.

00:24:18.910 --> 00:24:23.010
That’s why, today, we’re going to tell
you what they found out after the neutralization

00:24:23.010 --> 00:24:24.970
of SCP - 1730.

00:24:24.970 --> 00:24:28.960
Not only will we discover what’s become
of the many people involved, we learn about

00:24:28.960 --> 00:24:32.890
what happened in the last moments before the
neutralization took place.

00:24:32.890 --> 00:24:37.110
And perhaps most importantly of all, for the
sake of our universe, we will find out how

00:24:37.110 --> 00:24:42.370
Site 13 came into existence - and how Site
Director Emerson went down such a dark path.

00:24:42.370 --> 00:24:44.490
It’s time to get some answers.

00:24:44.490 --> 00:24:49.480
Welcome to the final part of the SCP - 1730
Saga, as we close the book on one of the most

00:24:49.480 --> 00:24:52.549
deadly locations in the Foundation multiverse.

00:24:52.549 --> 00:24:56.860
First to sit down in the interview chair was
Captain Ephram Ross, leader of Mobile Task

00:24:56.860 --> 00:24:59.300
Force Apollo 3 also known as The Game Wardens.

00:24:59.300 --> 00:25:04.530
He was a shaken man, looking far older than
his 35 years, his eyes heavy with the weight

00:25:04.530 --> 00:25:05.780
of the horrors he’d seen.

00:25:05.780 --> 00:25:10.230
He and his team were among the first to venture
into the bowels of Site 13 and witness the

00:25:10.230 --> 00:25:15.020
atrocities that’d gone on down there like
the Body Pit, full of fleshy slurry, or the

00:25:15.020 --> 00:25:19.900
countless containment chambers that marked
their occupants for vivisection and termination.

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:23.690
Captain Ross was haunted by the things that
had happened to his team under his watch such

00:25:23.690 --> 00:25:28.299
as the anomalous transformation of Houston’s
legs and the nightmarish warping death of

00:25:28.299 --> 00:25:31.820
Noah at the hands of a stretchy, reality-bending
anomaly.

00:25:31.820 --> 00:25:35.880
He compared the state of chaos going on down
there to something like Jurassic Park, where

00:25:35.880 --> 00:25:38.299
all hell had broken loose and the monsters
ruled.

00:25:38.299 --> 00:25:43.100
He also remarked on the Olympia Containment
Cells, each the size of a football stadium,

00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:47.650
capable of containing things far beyond the
scope of this universe’s SCP Foundation.

00:25:47.650 --> 00:25:52.070
His interviewer was the hard-nosed Dr. Peter
Vincent, who thanked Captain Ross for his

00:25:52.070 --> 00:25:56.470
contributions, and called in the next interview
subject: Agent Liam Ohalo, a Game Wardens

00:25:56.470 --> 00:25:59.240
Task Force member working under Captain Ross.

00:25:59.240 --> 00:26:03.820
He had a thousand yard stare, and even the
untrained observer could see that Agent Ohalo

00:26:03.820 --> 00:26:06.740
had left some part of himself back in Site
13.

00:26:06.740 --> 00:26:11.020
When Dr. Vincent attempted to interview him,
he mostly remained silent, only volunteering

00:26:11.020 --> 00:26:12.330
one grim sentiment:

00:26:12.330 --> 00:26:13.770
“We should’ve died in there.

00:26:13.770 --> 00:26:14.770
This isn’t real.

00:26:14.770 --> 00:26:15.770
This isn’t real.

00:26:15.770 --> 00:26:17.800
We were supposed to die in there.”

00:26:17.800 --> 00:26:22.580
Next to be interviewed was Captain Irantu
of Mobile Task Force Tau-5, aka Samsara.

00:26:22.580 --> 00:26:27.011
His interviewer, Dr. Isha Saint Claire, questioned
him about the nature of the mission, and the

00:26:27.011 --> 00:26:29.621
cybernetic soldier was even-keeled about the
matter.

00:26:29.621 --> 00:26:33.530
He said that, in spite of regrettable losses
of life, he was still satisfied with the outcome

00:26:33.530 --> 00:26:34.780
of the mission overall.

00:26:34.780 --> 00:26:39.860
The high-value targets were rescued, the anomaly
was - for all intents and purposes - neutralized,

00:26:39.860 --> 00:26:43.440
and the degree of loss was actually better
than their pre-mission predictions.

00:26:43.440 --> 00:26:47.010
It seems that the weight of death doesn’t
weigh quite as heavily on those who will probably

00:26:47.010 --> 00:26:51.500
never have to experience it, as the Samsara
team are capable of simply being rebooted

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:54.380
into new bodies if terminated in the field.

00:26:54.380 --> 00:26:56.720
People like Captain Hollis weren’t as lucky.

00:26:56.720 --> 00:27:00.840
Next, Agent Cotter Houston of the Game Wardens
was both interviewed and medically evaluated

00:27:00.840 --> 00:27:02.490
by Dr. Ian Harris.

00:27:02.490 --> 00:27:06.600
Agent Houston had his legs dematerialized
after he tripped into a rising tide of anomalous

00:27:06.600 --> 00:27:10.630
liquids - which he described as looking like
a moving, physical computer glitch.

00:27:10.630 --> 00:27:14.820
However, in spite of this, Agent Houston is
still able to stand and move of his own free

00:27:14.820 --> 00:27:15.820
will.

00:27:15.820 --> 00:27:19.440
It seemed to Dr. Harris that Houston’s legs
were somehow trapped between dimensions.

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:24.070
Houston told Dr. Harris that he didn’t experience
any kind of pain when his legs were removed,

00:27:24.070 --> 00:27:27.900
but to this day, he occasionally feels something
furry brushing up against them.

00:27:27.900 --> 00:27:30.740
Perhaps, wherever his legs are, they aren’t
alone...

00:27:30.740 --> 00:27:35.419
Next, the stoic Agent Munru of Samsara was
interviewed by Captain Elliott O’Neil of

00:27:35.419 --> 00:27:39.030
Mobile Task Force D-26, also known as Time
Cops.

00:27:39.030 --> 00:27:42.850
Captain O’Neil had a bone to pick with Munru
- namely, that he’d allowed Captain Hollis

00:27:42.850 --> 00:27:47.540
to run off and sacrifice her own life, despite
having a clear directive to prevent the human

00:27:47.540 --> 00:27:51.120
task force members from endangering themselves
at any cost.

00:27:51.120 --> 00:27:54.590
Munru deflected, claiming that when Hollis
separated from the group, he assumed that

00:27:54.590 --> 00:27:57.800
she ran off with intentions that never included
her own demise.

00:27:57.800 --> 00:28:02.100
O’Neil and the Foundation found this answer
unsatisfying, and decided to move on to their

00:28:02.100 --> 00:28:06.430
next interview with Onru - the last person
with Captain Hollis before her death.

00:28:06.430 --> 00:28:10.660
The interviewer, Dr. Darian Arnold, probed
the elite Samsara operative on why she turned

00:28:10.660 --> 00:28:15.179
off her camera before she and Hollis reached
the Thresher - the machine that Hollis overloaded

00:28:15.179 --> 00:28:17.720
to annihilate Site 13 from our dimension.

00:28:17.720 --> 00:28:21.660
She gave a more compelling answer than Munru:
When she and Hollis entered a server room

00:28:21.660 --> 00:28:25.669
on the way to the Thresher, they encountered
what may have been the ultimate cognitohazard:

00:28:25.669 --> 00:28:29.700
It was a vision of a terrifying alternate
dimension with billions dead.

00:28:29.700 --> 00:28:33.640
A poisoned star like the biblical wormwood
fell from the burning sky.

00:28:33.640 --> 00:28:38.480
A Nightmare God, like the one torturing Elliot
Emerson, wandered among fields of crucified

00:28:38.480 --> 00:28:41.480
people, covered in deadly, cognitohazardous
runes.

00:28:41.480 --> 00:28:46.240
Just looking at it burned the SCRAMBLE technology
out of Munru’s eyes, and she turned off

00:28:46.240 --> 00:28:49.830
her cameras to avoid potentially frying the
brains of mission control.

00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:51.570
Hollis wasn’t so lucky.

00:28:51.570 --> 00:28:55.530
The things she witnessed broke her sanity,
and when she finally overloaded the Thresher

00:28:55.530 --> 00:28:57.690
machine, she was laughing and crying.

00:28:57.690 --> 00:29:01.730
Finally, in perhaps the most enlightening
debriefing interview of them all, Site Director

00:29:01.730 --> 00:29:06.059
Willam Vesterland interviewed Dr. Mohammed
Scott - The highest-ranking researcher of

00:29:06.059 --> 00:29:10.700
Site 13, and confidant of the now-infamous
Director Elliot Emerson.

00:29:10.700 --> 00:29:14.760
The question was simple: just what had happened
for Site 13 to become so messed up?

00:29:14.760 --> 00:29:19.929
And Dr. Scott answered in detail, with a tale
of corruption, alternate realities, and the

00:29:19.929 --> 00:29:21.630
perils of unchecked power.

00:29:21.630 --> 00:29:26.000
In his home dimension, Site 13 was originally
created in Nome, Alaska to house the corpse

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:31.440
of a giant sea creature that beached itself
on the border of India and Bangladesh in 1964.

00:29:31.440 --> 00:29:35.450
It became the largest and most secretive Foundation
containment facility in the latter half of

00:29:35.450 --> 00:29:36.630
the 20th century.

00:29:36.630 --> 00:29:42.460
However, disaster struck in 1994, when a Marxist
extremist used an anomaly to level the Willis

00:29:42.460 --> 00:29:43.850
Tower in Chicago.

00:29:43.850 --> 00:29:47.970
As a result, the Foundation lost a lot of
its funding and international support, leaving

00:29:47.970 --> 00:29:49.659
it in dire financial straits.

00:29:49.659 --> 00:29:54.080
Enter the true villain of the Site 13 story:
Paul Manafort.

00:29:54.080 --> 00:29:58.190
If that name sounds familiar to you, it’s
because he was an associate of President Trump

00:29:58.190 --> 00:30:02.059
in our universe who got into legal trouble
for shady international dealings.

00:30:02.059 --> 00:30:06.120
However, in Dr. Scott’s universe, he was
a powerful staffer for President Bob Dole

00:30:06.120 --> 00:30:11.280
- who in that reality had beaten Bill Clinton
in the 1996 Presidential Election.

00:30:11.280 --> 00:30:16.000
Manafort was made the new Secretary General
of the Global Occult Coalition - The UN’s

00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:20.580
answer to the SCP Foundation, and one of their
leading competitors, with an ethos geared

00:30:20.580 --> 00:30:23.559
towards killing rather than containing anomalies.

00:30:23.559 --> 00:30:27.980
Manafort and the GOC co-opted the struggling
Foundation, providing them with money in exchange

00:30:27.980 --> 00:30:28.980
for control.

00:30:28.980 --> 00:30:31.900
The Foundation had no choice but to accept
this deal with the devil.

00:30:31.900 --> 00:30:35.940
Slowly, Manafort replaced the Foundation old
guard with toadies and loyalists.

00:30:35.940 --> 00:30:39.299
The Ethics Committee and the O5 command were
dismantled.

00:30:39.299 --> 00:30:42.960
Dissenters were dragged out of their offices
and shot point blank in the head, execution-style.

00:30:42.960 --> 00:30:48.480
Site 13 had originally been directed by Dr.
Bright, but Bright was arrested and contained

00:30:48.480 --> 00:30:53.260
under false pretences so Manafort could install
a new director: A mid-level researcher by

00:30:53.260 --> 00:30:55.039
the name of Elliot Emerson.

00:30:55.039 --> 00:30:59.660
Emerson is often painted as a sadistic monster
who took pleasure in torturing anomalies to

00:30:59.660 --> 00:31:02.110
death and flushing them down the body pit.

00:31:02.110 --> 00:31:07.470
The reality is both simpler and more grim:
Emerson, it turns out, was just an eager yes

00:31:07.470 --> 00:31:08.470
man.

00:31:08.470 --> 00:31:12.390
He was put into his position to follow Manafort’s
orders to a tee, and those orders were simple

00:31:12.390 --> 00:31:13.430
- Kill.

00:31:13.430 --> 00:31:18.149
In a perfect example of the banality of evil,
Director Emerson converted Site 13 into a

00:31:18.149 --> 00:31:22.250
brutal slaughterhouse, just as his overlords
at the GOC had ordered him.

00:31:22.250 --> 00:31:25.880
But things were quickly getting out of hand,
and one of the most vocal critics of the new

00:31:25.880 --> 00:31:30.899
regime was one of Emerson’s old lovers,
one Dr. Vera Hadley, Assistant Director of

00:31:30.899 --> 00:31:32.179
Anomalous Biology.

00:31:32.179 --> 00:31:37.260
Dr. Hadley was disgusted by the inhuman acts
Emerson was carrying out and couldn’t stay

00:31:37.260 --> 00:31:40.600
silent, and for this she faced horrific consequences.

00:31:40.600 --> 00:31:43.890
Corrupt guards stripped her and beat her to
within an inch of her life in front of her

00:31:43.890 --> 00:31:44.909
co-workers.

00:31:44.909 --> 00:31:47.020
In that moment, she swore her revenge.

00:31:47.020 --> 00:31:51.060
She sabotaged the containment procedures and
had the engineers rig the already unstable

00:31:51.060 --> 00:31:52.840
Thresher device to overload.

00:31:52.840 --> 00:31:57.570
As Emerson watched the anomalies break containment
he began to fear for his life - both from

00:31:57.570 --> 00:32:01.770
the anomalies themselves, and from the punishments
of his superiors at the GOC.

00:32:01.770 --> 00:32:05.210
Dr. Scott revealed that Emerson was no evil
mastermind.

00:32:05.210 --> 00:32:06.770
He was a lapdog for the GOC.

00:32:06.770 --> 00:32:09.141
A dirty coward, all the way to the very end.

00:32:09.141 --> 00:32:10.860
And he was desperate.

00:32:10.860 --> 00:32:15.260
He held Dr. Scott at gunpoint and ordered
him to activate the Thresher or die, and the

00:32:15.260 --> 00:32:16.370
rest is history.

00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:20.360
There would be no redemption for Dr. Scott’s
former friend, as Emerson ended up chained

00:32:20.360 --> 00:32:24.750
to the rune-covered, platform head of a Nightmare
God for all eternity.

00:32:24.750 --> 00:32:29.820
So ends the debriefing of the Site 13 survivors,
and closes the book on that terrible place

00:32:29.820 --> 00:32:31.390
- for now, anyway.

00:32:31.390 --> 00:32:36.200
The story of SCP - 1730 is anything but simple,
and there are so many angles from which this

00:32:36.200 --> 00:32:39.530
dark tragedy of cruelty and corruption can
be approached.

00:32:39.530 --> 00:32:44.010
And ultimately, it was all for the same two
things at the root of every evil: The desire

00:32:44.010 --> 00:32:45.750
for money and power.

00:32:45.750 --> 00:32:50.340
But the pursuit of these base desires can
lead to some truly nightmarish consequences,

00:32:50.340 --> 00:32:54.520
and nobody knows this better than former Director
Elliot Emerson - who’ll be paying for these

00:32:54.520 --> 00:32:57.850
sins until the end of time, and perhaps even
beyond.

00:32:57.850 --> 00:33:03.130
Now go check out another epic tale from the
SCP Foundation, SCP-5000 - The Suit.

